[2026-07-31T06:41:40.495Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=3875d76c80ae0eb4ed297b1fe3b8e225]   Trigger:   The site navbar needed a visual refresh to match a dark UI direction, replacing its light-mode-first styling with a consistently dark look.
[2026-07-31T06:41:40.495Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=3875d76c80ae0eb4ed297b1fe3b8e225]   Response:  - Updated the Logo component with richer gradient tones (violet-to-cyan), added subtle borders and shadows to the icon badge, and switched the wordmark to plain white with a cyan hover state instead of dark-mode-conditional zinc classes.
- Reworked NavLinks active/hover states to use slate backgrounds and cyan highlights (including a glowing active-page dot indicator) and cleaned up unnecessary blank lines and wrapper divs.
- Restyled the Navbar header bar (slate background, heavier blur/shadow, updated skeleton loader) and UserMenu (login/register buttons, dropdown menu, avatar border, and menu items) to use a slate/cyan palette instead of zinc-based light/dark variants; also removed a leftover debug console.log statement.
[2026-07-31T06:41:40.495Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=3875d76c80ae0eb4ed297b1fe3b8e225]   Decisions: - **Fixed dark theme over dual light/dark support**: Instead of maintaining conditional `dark:` variant classes throughout the navbar components, the styling was consolidated to a single slate-based dark palette, simplifying the class lists and guaranteeing visual consistency without relying on system/user theme toggles.
- **Cyan as the primary accent color**: Active links, focus rings, hover borders, and highlight glows were switched from indigo to cyan tones, giving interactive elements stronger visual contrast against the darker background.
